# Tests and regressions

Every area must have regression tests. A change is incomplete without them.

- Bug fixes: add a test that fails before the fix and passes after.
- SMTP: greeting, MAIL/RCPT/DATA, AUTH, SIZE, hidden extensions, limits.
- MIME: fixtures for multipart, encodings, attachments, CID, malformed input.
- REST: OpenAPI contract tests. MCP: protocol tests plus REST/MCP parity tests.
- Config: valid, invalid, unknown fields, env/flag overlay, MailDev outgoing flags (default off).
- Comparison lab: REST + UI vs live MailDev when touching ingest, REST, UI, or relay.
- UI operator paths: Playwright (or equivalent), not screenshot-only.
- Do not delete or weaken a test to make CI pass unless it is provably wrong; document why.
- Do not mark a task complete on manual testing alone.
